<title>SOUTH KOREA: Yukong to expand petrol sales to Japan.</title>
<headline>Yukong to expand petrol sales to Japan.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Yukong Ltd said on Wednesday it planned to export 700,000 barrels of petrol to Japan in 1997 versus 600,000 barrels in 1996.  </p>
<p>A Yukong statement said exports to Zen-noh, Japan's Nationwide Federation of Agricultural Cooperatives, would remain unchanged at last year's 400,000 barrels.</p>
<p>Yukong will sell the remaining 300,000 barrels to Japan's distribution, trade and refining companies.</p>
<p>Japan liberalised imports of oil products from 1996 and Yukong says it was the first South Korean refiner to export petrol to Japan.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
